<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 19 May, from 639 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">639 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,387 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ashina Jiesheshuai and his tribesmen attack Emperor Taizong</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashina-clan">Ashina</a> Jiesheshuai, a member of the Ashina clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-turkic-khaganate">Eastern Turkic Khaganate</a> and a general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a>, led his tribesmen in an assault on Emperor Taizong at Jiucheng Palace. He died the same day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Emperor Taizong of Tang</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">715 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,311 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gregory II begins his pontificate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gregory II began his pontificate as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. His defiance of the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iii-the-isaurian">Leo III the Isaurian</a> in the iconoclastic controversy eventually led to the establishment of the popes' temporal power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ii">Pope Gregory II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iii-the-isaurian">Leo III the Isaurian</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">Papacy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/934">934 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,092 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Kourkouas takes Melitene for the Byzantine Empire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Besieged by the Byzantine general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-kourkouas">John Kourkouas</a>, Melitene (modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malatya">Malatya</a>) surrendered, compelled by hunger after many inhabitants had abandoned it. Kourkouas let only Christians or converts remain, and the city was fully incorporated into the empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-kourkouas">John Kourkouas</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malatya">Malatya</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/france" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1051 CE <span class="tih-ago">975 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry I of France marries Anna of Kiev</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, seeking a third wife further afield, married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anna-of-kiev">Anna of Kiev</a>, a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-the-wise">Yaroslav the Wise</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>. She later ruled as regent for their son Philip I after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s death in 1060.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anna-of-kiev">Anna of Kiev</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1536">1536 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">490 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anne Boleyn is beheaded at the Tower of London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s second queen, mother of the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>, was executed by a French swordsman on charges widely seen as fabricated. Henry was betrothed to Jane Seymour the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1643">1643 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">383 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French victory at Rocroi breaks Spain's military reputation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The young Duke of Enghien, later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-grand-conde">Great Condé</a>, defeated the Spanish army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rocroi">Rocroi</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The defeat of the famed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tercio">tercios</a> signalled the decline of Spanish power on land.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1649">1649 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">377 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">England is declared a Commonwealth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four months after the execution of Charles I, the Rump Parliament declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> a 'Commonwealth and Free State' without king or House of Lords. It gave way to Cromwell's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> in 1653.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1935">1935 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">91 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">T. E. Lawrence dies after a motorcycle crash</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/t-e-lawrence">T. E. Lawrence</a>, 'Lawrence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>', died six days after crashing near his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorset">Dorset</a> cottage. He had served with the Arab Revolt and wrote Seven Pillars of Wisdom.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1994">1994 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis dies in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former First Lady died aged 64. Her composure after her husband's assassination in 1963 made her an enduring public figure, and she later worked as a book editor.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li></ol>
